<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_part">Part I </span>Appendix</h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivations and proofs</h3>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide detailed derivations and proofs for the background and the claims made in the paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of <math id="A1.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrization</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by defining the optimal denoiser for the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> parameterization we use in the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal denoiser <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> for a data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> at a particular
noise level <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of the loss function</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f}\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>f</mi></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f}\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}=1-\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}=1-\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\left\{x_{0}^{i}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\left\{x_{0}^{i}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite empirical distribution,
the optimal denoiser <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> has the following analytical expression:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}(x,t)=\sum_{i}x_{0}^{i}\softmax_{i}\left\{-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{j}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">softmax</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}(x,t)=\sum_{i}x_{0}^{i}\softmax_{i}\left\{-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{j}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first write down the objective (<a href="#A1.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Definition A.1. ‣ A.1 Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of ϵ and 𝑥_0 parametrization ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) in terms of the
random variable <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(x,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(x,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-n}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left\lVert f(x,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mi>dx</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-n}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left\lVert f(x,t)-x_{0}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We then minimize the integral coordinate-wise for each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to get the
optimal <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)(\hat{f}(x,t)-x_{0})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)(\hat{f}(x,t)-x_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}x_{0}^{i}\exp(-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{i}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})}{\sum_{j}\exp(-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{j}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i}x_{0}^{i}\exp(-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{i}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})}{\sum_{j}\exp(-\left\lVert x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}^{j}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\softmax_{i}\left\{a_{j}\right\}_{j\in[N]}=\frac{\exp(a_{i})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(a_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>softmax</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\softmax_{i}\left\{a_{j}\right\}_{j\in[N]}=\frac{\exp(a_{i})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(a_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get (<a href="#A1.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proposition A.2. ‣ A.1 Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of ϵ and 𝑥_0 parametrization ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal denoiser <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}(z,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}(z,t)</annotation></semantics></math> for a data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> at a particular
noise level <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of the loss function</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f}\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-\epsilon\right\lVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>f</mi></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f}\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-\epsilon\right\lVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\left\{x_{0}^{i}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\left\{x_{0}^{i}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite empirical distribution,
the optimal denoiser for the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-parameterization <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math>
can be written in terms of that of the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-parameterization <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\epsilon}(x,t)=(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\hat{f}(x,t))/\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\epsilon}(x,t)=(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\hat{f}(x,t))/\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We follow the same proof as <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition A.2. ‣ A.1 Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of ϵ and 𝑥_0 parametrization ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, with the main difference being the following step:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-\epsilon\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\left\lVert f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon,t)-\epsilon\right\lVert_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(x,t)-(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0})/\sigma_{t}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)\end{subarray}}\left\lVert f(x,t)-(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0})/\sigma_{t}\right\lVert_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Another way to prove <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition A.2. ‣ A.1 Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of ϵ and 𝑥_0 parametrization ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> and
<a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition A.4. ‣ A.1 Optimal denoiser: derivation, equivalence of ϵ and 𝑥_0 parametrization ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> is to show that the optimal solutions are of the
form <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[x_{0}\mid x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[x_{0}\mid x]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[\epsilon\mid x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[\epsilon\mid x]</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim N(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0},\sigma_{t}I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it becomes clear that the two
expressions are linearly related to each other.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn to the patch-based denoiser, incorporating both locality and equivariance constraints into the optimal denoising problem as suggested in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, repeating the derivations in the notations of this manuscript.
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{x_{0}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{x_{0}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite empirical distribution of images, and let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}^{q}:\R^{d\times d}\to\R^{d\times d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}^{q}:\R^{d\times d}\to\R^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the operator that masks out a <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\times p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\times p</annotation></semantics></math> patch centered at pixel <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, setting the rest of the pixels to 0.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As suggested in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, we impose two constraints on each patch-wise function <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">1. <em id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Locality:</em></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}(x,t)\;=\;f^{q}\bigl(M_{t}^{q}\,x,\,t\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}(x,t)\;=\;f^{q}\bigl(M_{t}^{q}\,x,\,t\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">2. <em id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Equivariance:</em> For every 2D translation <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in T(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in T(2)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\bigl(g\circ x,\,t\bigr)\;=\;g\circ f(x,t),\quad\Longrightarrow\quad f^{q}\bigl(g\circ x,t\bigr)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x,t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\bigl(g\circ x,\,t\bigr)\;=\;g\circ f(x,t),\quad\Longrightarrow\quad f^{q}\bigl(g\circ x,t\bigr)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x,t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">i.e. denoising commutes with the action of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(2)</annotation></semantics></math> and relocates patches accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The patch-based optimal denoiser <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> for a data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> at a particular
noise level <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of the loss function</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>f</mi></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{\,x_{0}\sim X,\;\epsilon\sim N(0,I),\;t\sim[0,1]}\bigl\|f\bigl(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\,\epsilon,\;t\bigr)-x_{0}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{\,x_{0}\sim X,\;\epsilon\sim N(0,I),\;t\sim[0,1]}\bigl\|f\bigl(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\,\epsilon,\;t\bigr)-x_{0}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{q}(x,t)=f^{q}\bigl(M_{t}^{q}x,\,t\bigr),\quad q=1,\dots,Q,\quad\quad\text{~~~~~~~~~~~~(locality)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> (locality)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{q}(x,t)=f^{q}\bigl(M_{t}^{q}x,\,t\bigr),\quad q=1,\dots,Q,\quad\quad\text{~~~~~~~~~~~~(locality)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f\bigl(g\circ x,\,t\bigr)=g\circ f(x,t),\quad\forall\,g\in T(2).\quad\quad\text{(equivariance)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(equivariance)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f\bigl(g\circ x,\,t\bigr)=g\circ f(x,t),\quad\forall\,g\in T(2).\quad\quad\text{(equivariance)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Patch-based optimal denoiser)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the empirical distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{x_{0}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{x_{0}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{f}^{q}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{f}^{q}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Definition A.6. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> is given, for each patch location <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)\;=\;\sum_{i}\sum_{g\in T(2)}\;\left(g\circ x_{0}^{i}\right)^{q}\;\softmax_{i}\Bigl(-\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\bigl\|\,M_{t}^{q}\left(x\;-\;\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,g\circ x_{0}^{i}\right)\bigr\|^{2}\Bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">softmax</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)\;=\;\sum_{i}\sum_{g\in T(2)}\;\left(g\circ x_{0}^{i}\right)^{q}\;\softmax_{i}\Bigl(-\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\bigl\|\,M_{t}^{q}\left(x\;-\;\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,g\circ x_{0}^{i}\right)\bigr\|^{2}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the full-image denoiser is obtained by reconstructing the final image from the pixels above.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this result in three steps: (1) decomposition into per-pixel optimization, (2) equivalence of equivariance constraint and data augmentation, and (3) derivation of the local form.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Decomposition into per-pixel optimization.<span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the operator that extracts pixel <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> from an image, and define <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{q}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{q}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> places a scalar value at pixel <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and zeros elsewhere. Since pixels are disjoint, <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}P_{j}^{T}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}P_{j}^{T}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, making <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{q}P_{q}^{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{q}P_{q}^{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal projections with <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By orthogonality of pixel projections:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(x)-x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(x)-x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}(f(x)-x_{0})\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|\sum_{q=1}^{Q}P_{q}P_{q}^{T}(f(x)-x_{0})\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\|P_{q}f(x)-P_{q}x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\|P_{q}f(x)-P_{q}x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}|f^{q}(x)-x_{0}^{q}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}|f^{q}(x)-x_{0}^{q}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the original minimization problem decomposes as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\|f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>f</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\|f(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\min_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}^{q}\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\min_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}^{q}\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each pixel can be optimized independently.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Equivariance constraint equals data augmentation.<span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For the <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-th pixel problem with equivariance constraint:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.EGx18.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.EGx18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{rl}\min_{f^{q}}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}^{q}\right]^{2}\\[8.5359pt]
\text{s.t. }&amp;f^{q}(g\circ x)=(g\circ f(x))^{q}\quad\forall g\in T(2)\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>min</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mtext>s.t. </mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{rl}\min_{f^{q}}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-x_{0}^{q}\right]^{2}\\[8.5359pt]
\text{s.t. }&amp;f^{q}(g\circ x)=(g\circ f(x))^{q}\quad\forall g\in T(2)\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The equivariance constraint implies that for any translation <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A1.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}(g\circ x)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}(g\circ x)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider the data-augmented problem:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(g\circ(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon))-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(g\circ(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon))-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We want to prove that (<a href="#A1.EGx18" title="Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>) is equivalent to (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). To do so, we first show that the optimal solution of (<a href="#A1.EGx18" title="Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>) does not change with data-augmentation, then show that the optimal solution of (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) satisfies the equivariance constraint.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Constrained optima invariant under data-augmentation</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since translation commutes with noise addition and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g\circ x_{0})^{q}=x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g\circ x_{0})^{q}=x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#A1.EGx18" title="Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>) under data-augmentation becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f^{q}}\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f^{q}}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(g\circ x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(g\circ x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{q}(g\circ x)=(g\circ f(x))^{q}\quad\forall g\in T(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{q}(g\circ x)=(g\circ f(x))^{q}\quad\forall g\in T(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the equivariance constraint, then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}(g\circ x)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}(g\circ x)=f^{g^{-1}q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I),g\sim T(2)}\left(f^{q}(g\circ x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I),g\sim T(2)}\left(f^{q}(g\circ x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon,g}\left(f^{g^{-1}q}(x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon,g}\left(f^{g^{-1}q}(x)-x_{0}^{g^{-1}q}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon}\sum_{r=1}^{Q}\left(f^{r}(x)-x_{0}^{r}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon}\sum_{r=1}^{Q}\left(f^{r}(x)-x_{0}^{r}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon}\left(f^{q}(x)-x_{0}^{q}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\argmin_{f^{q}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{0},\epsilon}\left(f^{q}(x)-x_{0}^{q}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data-augmented optima is equivariant</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can solve the data-augmented problem (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof of Patch-based optimal denoiser. ‣ A.2 Patch-based optimal denoiser: formal derivation ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) and check that its optimal solution <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivariant under the transformation <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\rightarrow h\circ x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\rightarrow h\circ x</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in T(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in T(2)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(h\circ x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(h\circ x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|h\circ x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|h\circ x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(h^{-1}\circ g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(h^{-1}\circ g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g^{\prime}\in T(2)}(h\circ g^{\prime}\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g^{\prime}}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g^{\prime}\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g^{\prime}\in T(2)}(h\circ g^{\prime}\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g^{\prime}}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g^{\prime}\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(h\circ f(x))^{q}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(h\circ f(x))^{q},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}=h^{-1}\circ g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}=h^{-1}\circ g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Local form derivation.</span>
From the data augmentation equivalence, the optimal denoiser for pixel <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\mathbb{E}_{g\sim T(2)}\left[f^{q}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing the objective as an integral over <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,g\sim T(2)}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,g\sim T(2)}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">With the locality constraint <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}(x)=f^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}(x)=f^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can “integrate out” the coordinates of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> that are masked out by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on them), to get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,g\sim T(2)}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-p^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert M^{q}_{t}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x)\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(M^{q}_{t}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,d(M^{q}_{t}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim X,g\sim T(2)}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-p^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert M^{q}_{t}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x)\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(M^{q}_{t}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,d(M^{q}_{t}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Solving for the optimal <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
g\sim T(2)\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)\quad(f^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{\begin{subarray}{c}x_{0}\sim X\\
g\sim T(2)\\
\epsilon\sim N(0,I)\end{subarray}}\exp\left(-\frac{\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)\quad(f^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Rearranging:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(M_{t}^{q}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\exp\left(-\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{h\in T(2)}\exp\left(-\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(h\circ x_{0}^{j})\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\exp\left(-\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{h\in T(2)}\exp\left(-\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(h\circ x_{0}^{j})\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Using the softmax notation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|M_{t}^{q}x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}M_{t}^{q}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide justification for our algorithm provided in the main paper.
In particular, we formally justify why it makes sense to binarize the sensitivity fields into a mask of zeros and ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At first, we generalize the patch-based optimal denoiser by relaxing the locality constraint.
Instead of restricting to patch extraction operators <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider linear operators <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> that can capture more complex spatial relationships.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalized masked optimal denoiser)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The generalized masked optimal denoiser <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> for a data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> at noise level <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizer of:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f}\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>f</mi></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f}\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E_{\,x_{0}\sim X,\;\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\bigl\|f\bigl(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\,\epsilon,\;t\bigr)-x_{0}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E_{\,x_{0}\sim X,\;\epsilon\sim N(0,I)}\bigl\|f\bigl(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\,\epsilon,\;t\bigr)-x_{0}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex35.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f^{q}(x,t)=f^{q}\bigl(A_{t}^{q}x,\,t\bigr),\quad q=1,\dots,Q," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{q}(x,t)=f^{q}\bigl(A_{t}^{q}x,\,t\bigr),\quad q=1,\dots,Q,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(generalized locality)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f\bigl(g\;\circ\;x,\,t\bigr)=g\;\circ\;f(x,t),\quad\forall\,g\in T(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">∘</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f\bigl(g\;\circ\;x,\,t\bigr)=g\;\circ\;f(x,t),\quad\forall\,g\in T(2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(equivariance)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear operator.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that when <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is effectively unconstrained (i.e. there is no locality). On the other hand, when <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. The following result interpolates between these two extreme cases, showing that the optimal denoiser depends only on the row-space <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalized masked optimal denoiser)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Following the decomposition and data augmentation equivalence from the previous section, the optimal denoiser for pixel <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> under the generalized locality constraint is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert P_{t}^{q}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert P_{t}^{q}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}^{q}=(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\left(A_{t}^{q}(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\right)^{\dagger}A_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}^{q}=(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\left(A_{t}^{q}(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\right)^{\dagger}A_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projection matrix onto the row space of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The objective (<a href="#A1.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Definition A.8 (Generalized masked optimal denoiser). ‣ A.3 Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>dx</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}(x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We use SVD to write <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}=U^{T}\Lambda V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}=U^{T}\Lambda V</annotation></semantics></math>, and notice that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}^{q}=V\Lambda^{\dagger}V^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}^{q}=V\Lambda^{\dagger}V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix with 0 or 1 diagonal entries depending if the corresponding diagonal entry of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero. Then we impose the constraint <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}(x)=f^{q}(A_{t}^{q}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}(x)=f^{q}(A_{t}^{q}x)</annotation></semantics></math> and perform a change of variables <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=Vx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=Vx</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}A_{t}^{q}}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">A</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">q</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>dx</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}g\circ x_{0}-x\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}A_{t}^{q}}x)-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0})-{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda y})-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}dy}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">y</mi><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">dy</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0})-{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}\right\lVert^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda y})-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}dy},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we have absorbed <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> as it is an invertible matrix. Next, we integrate out the coordinates of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the zero-values in <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and absorb non-zero entries of <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, to get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0})-{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}\right)^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right\lVert\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}y})-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}dy}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">†</mo></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">dy</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\E_{x_{0},g}\left(\sigma_{t}\sqrt{2\pi}\right)^{-d^{2}}\exp\left(-\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0})-{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}\right)^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2}\right\lVert\right)\left(f^{q}({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}y})-(g\circ x_{0})^{q}\right)^{2}\,{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}dy}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We then solve for the optimal <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}^{q}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}^{q}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and change variables to get <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}^{q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}^{q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(y,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(y,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}}\left({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">†</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">y</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}}\left({\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}y}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}V}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}V}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">†</mo></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">V</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}\Lambda^{\dagger}V}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}P_{t}^{q}}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#CC0000;" mathcolor="#CC0000">q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\left\lVert{\color[rgb]{0.8,0,0}P_{t}^{q}}\left(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})\right)\right\lVert^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.9.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Diagonal operators and mask binarization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}=diag(a^{q}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}=diag(a^{q}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is further constrained to be diagonal matrix with entries <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal denoiser simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|B^{q}\odot(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i}))\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|B^{q}\odot(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i}))\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary mask with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{q}_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{q}_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{q}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{q}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{q}_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{q}_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.Thmcorollary1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes element-wise multiplication.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin with the generalized optimal denoiser from equation (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proposition A.9 (Generalized masked optimal denoiser). ‣ A.3 Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and substitute the diagonal operator <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}=\text{diag}(a^{q}_{1},a^{q}_{2},\ldots,a^{q}_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}=\text{diag}(a^{q}_{1},a^{q}_{2},\ldots,a^{q}_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}^{q}=(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\left(A_{t}^{q}(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\right)^{\dagger}A_{t}^{q}=B^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}^{q}=(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\left(A_{t}^{q}(A_{t}^{q})^{T}\right)^{\dagger}A_{t}^{q}=B^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. We get a binary mask because oefficients <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> cancel out completely when <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The actual values of non-zero <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> do not affect the optimal denoiser—only whether <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> matters. Then we can apply <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition A.9 (Generalized masked optimal denoiser). ‣ A.3 Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a> to get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|B^{q}\odot(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i}))\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}^{q}(x,t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{g\in T(2)}(g\circ x_{0}^{i})^{q}\cdot\text{softmax}_{i,g}\left\{-\frac{1}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|B^{q}\odot(x-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}(g\circ x_{0}^{i}))\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof, showing that the optimal denoiser depends only on the binary support of the diagonal operator, not on the specific non-zero values.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connection to patch-based denoiser:</span> When <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding pixel <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is effectively removed from the optimization, as it contributes zero to the distance metric. This is precisely the locality constraint from the patch-based denoiser: pixels outside the patch (where <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{q}_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{q}_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) do not influence the denoising of pixel <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Justification for binary masks)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In summary, we showed in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition A.9 (Generalized masked optimal denoiser). ‣ A.3 Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a> that the only interesting generalized locality matrices are binary masks. In particular, when the masking operator <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> has a diagonal structure, the specific values of the non-zero entries cancel out in the softmax computation. This means that:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal denoiser depends only on the pixels that are included in the mask (the support), not their relative weights.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Binary masks </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are as expressive as any diagonal weighting scheme for this optimization problem.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This theoretical result justifies our practical choice of binary masks in the main paper, as more complex weighting provides no additional benefit for the optimal denoiser.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>“Pass-through” denoisers: detailed analysis of SNR</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed analysis of the signal-to-noise ratio in the principal components of the data, extending section “Pass-through” denoisers in the main paper.
Let’s consider the data matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=[x_{0}^{1}x_{0}^{2}\ldots x_{0}^{N}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=[x_{0}^{1}x_{0}^{2}\ldots x_{0}^{N}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Doing singular value decomposition, and assuming <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq d</annotation></semantics></math> we get <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=U\text{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots\lambda_{d})V^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=U\text{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots\lambda_{d})V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are sorted in the descending order of their absolute values.
Covariance of the dataset, assuming that the mean of the dataset is zero:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}XX^{T}=\frac{1}{N}U\text{diag}(\lambda_{1}^{2},\lambda_{2}^{2},\ldots\lambda_{d}^{2})U^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}XX^{T}=\frac{1}{N}U\text{diag}(\lambda_{1}^{2},\lambda_{2}^{2},\ldots\lambda_{d}^{2})U^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> are the principal components of the data and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}^{2}/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}^{2}/N</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of the data along those components.
We can now compute the signal-to-noise ratio along each of the principal components of the data:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{SNR}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\left(U_{i}^{T}\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}\right)^{2}\right]}{\E_{\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)}\left[\left(U_{i}^{T}\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon\right)^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\E_{x_{0}\sim X}\left[\left(U_{i}^{T}\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}x_{0}\right)^{2}\right]}{\E_{\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)}\left[\left(U_{i}^{T}\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon\right)^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\cdot U_{i}^{T}\Sigma U_{i}}{(1-\alpha_{t})\cdot U_{i}^{T}U_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\cdot U_{i}^{T}\Sigma U_{i}}{(1-\alpha_{t})\cdot U_{i}^{T}U_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\cdot\lambda_{i}^{2}/N}{1-\alpha_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\cdot\lambda_{i}^{2}/N}{1-\alpha_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}^{2}/N\gg(1-\alpha_{t})/\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}^{2}/N\gg(1-\alpha_{t})/\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the intrinsic data variance is much larger than the relative noise level, and the signal was not “destroyed” by noise.
Note, the analysis above does not have to be performed on the entire dataset, but rather on the most relevant set of neighbors to the image that is currently being denoised.
In that case, the high SNR projections will be more precise and specific to each particular image as long as SVD is well defined.
Due to computation constraints and to keep the analysis simple from now on we will assume that the covariance matrix is computed on the entire dataset.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Manipulating the sensitivity field: variance of the perturbation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the derivation for the variance of the added perturbation <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> in the section “Manipulating the sensitivity field” of the main paper.
Denote by <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\gamma cs" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\gamma cs</annotation></semantics></math> the signal vector; then the empirical covariance of the modified data is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\rm mod}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>mod</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\rm mod}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E[\hat{x}_{0}\hat{x}_{0}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E[\hat{x}_{0}\hat{x}_{0}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E[(x_{0}+\gamma cs)(x_{0}+\gamma cs)^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>cs</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>cs</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E[(x_{0}+\gamma cs)(x_{0}+\gamma cs)^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\E[x_{0}x_{0}^{T}]+\gamma\E[x_{0}s^{T}c^{T}]+\gamma\E[cs^{T}x_{0}^{T}]+\gamma^{2}\E[css^{T}c^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>cs</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>css</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E[x_{0}x_{0}^{T}]+\gamma\E[x_{0}s^{T}c^{T}]+\gamma\E[cs^{T}x_{0}^{T}]+\gamma^{2}\E[css^{T}c^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\gamma^{2}\E[cc^{T}]ss^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>orig</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>ss</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\gamma^{2}\E[cc^{T}]ss^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\gamma^{2}\frac{1}{3}I_{3}\otimes ss^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>orig</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\gamma^{2}\frac{1}{3}I_{3}\otimes ss^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we used <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[x_{0}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[x_{0}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[c]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[c]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and for <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\sim\text{Uniform}([-1,1]^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\sim\text{Uniform}([-1,1]^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[cc^{T}]=\frac{1}{3}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[cc^{T}]=\frac{1}{3}I</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the noisy observations <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\hat{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\hat{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the covariance becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{\rm mod}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>mod</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{\rm mod}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\E[\hat{x}_{t}\hat{x}_{t}^{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\E[\hat{x}_{t}\hat{x}_{t}^{T}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\E[\hat{x}_{0}\hat{x}_{0}^{T}]+(1-\alpha_{t})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\E[\hat{x}_{0}\hat{x}_{0}^{T}]+(1-\alpha_{t})I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\Sigma_{\rm mod}+(1-\alpha_{t})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>mod</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\Sigma_{\rm mod}+(1-\alpha_{t})I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\frac{1}{3}I_{3}\otimes ss^{T}+(1-\alpha_{t})I." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>orig</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{t}\Sigma_{\rm orig}+\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\frac{1}{3}I_{3}\otimes ss^{T}+(1-\alpha_{t})I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming the RGB perturbation affects each color channel independently and focusing on a single channel, the second term contributes a rank-1 perturbation with eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{W}^{2}=\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{W}^{2}=\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By the Wiener filter analysis of <a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="Connection to Gaussian data and linear denoiser. ‣ 3 Deriving Denoising Sensitivity from Dataset Statistics ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the learned sensitivity along the new "W" principal component is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{w}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{w}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\lambda_{W}^{2}}{\lambda_{W}^{2}+(1-\alpha_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\lambda_{W}^{2}}{\lambda_{W}^{2}+(1-\alpha_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3}{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3+(1-\alpha_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3}{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}/3+(1-\alpha_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}}{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}+3(1-\alpha_{t})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}}{\alpha_{t}\gamma^{2}\|s\|^{2}+3(1-\alpha_{t})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the noise variance at timestep <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiments and Ablation </h3>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Ablation of our model</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The analytical model proposed in this paper has a single hyperparameter: <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> – the threshold of the sensitivity field binarization.
In <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Ours: why do we binarize the sensitivity field ‣ Appendix A Derivations and proofs ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> we formally justify binarization of the sensitivity fields for our analytical model.
Here, we demonstrate the effect of choosing different binarization thresholds.
In particular, from <a href="#A2.F6" title="In B.1 Ablation of our model ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments and Ablation ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we can see that higher threshold values (i.e., smaller patch sizes) correspond to a sharper, but “patchier”.
On the other side, small threshold values (i.e., bigger patch sizes) cause the generated image to be over-smoothed.
We report the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and MSE metrics of correlation with the trained diffusion model for different threshold values in  <a href="#A2.T2" title="In B.1 Ablation of our model ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments and Ablation ‣ Part I Appendix ‣ Locality in Image Diffusion ModelsEmerges from Data Statistics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table">
